{"acceptance_length": 6.535211267605634, "acceptance_lengths": [11, 5, 2, 6, 2, 5, 4, 4, 5, 2, 3, 8, 4, 3, 4, 4, 3, 3, 4, 4, 16, 2, 3, 2, 16, 6, 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 2, 1, 1, 16, 4, 12, 3, 3, 14, 8, 16, 16, 16, 9, 16, 16, 16, 5, 14, 4, 1, 3, 8, 6, 1, 5, 16, 8, 11, 16, 10, 5, 8, 9, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 4], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23463925248, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23463915520, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "To solve the problem of finding the **minimum difference** between any two elements in a given array, we can follow these steps:\n\n### Steps:\n1. **Sort the array**: Sorting helps us compare adjacent elements, which will give us the minimum difference.\n2. **Iterate through the sorted array**: Compare each element with the next one and keep track of the minimum difference found.\n\n### Example:\nFor the input `(1, 5, 3, 19, 18, 25)`:\n- After sorting: `(1, 3, 5, 18, 19, 25)`\n- Differences: `2, 2, 13, 1, 6`\n- Minimum difference is `1`\n\n### Python Function:\n\n```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr, n):\n    # Sort the array\n    arr = sorted(arr)\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    \n    # Iterate through the array to find the minimum difference\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = arr[i + 1] - arr[i]\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n    \n    return min_diff\n```\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert find_min_diff((1,5,3,19,18,25),6) == 1\nassert find_min_diff((4,3,2,6),4) == 1\nassert find_min_diff((30,5,20,9),4) == 4\n```\n\n### Explanation of Test Cases:\n- `(1,5,3,19,18,25)` \u2192 sorted \u2192 `(1,3,5,18,19,25)` \u2192 min diff is `19 - 18 = 1`\n- `(4,3,2,6)` \u2192 sorted \u2192 `(2,3,4,6)` \u2192 min diff is `3 - 2 = 1`\n- `(30,5,20,9)` \u2192 sorted \u2192 `(5,9,20,30)` \u2192 min diff is `9 - 5 = 4`\n\n\u2705 All assertions will pass with this implementation.", "decode_seconds": 2.7849994990974665, "draft_calls": 71, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 137, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash":