\n```\n\n---\n\n### Test Cases:\n\n```python\nassert find_length(\"11000010001\") == 6\nassert find_length(\"10111\") == 1\nassert find_length(\"11011101100101\") == 2\n```\n\n---\n\n### Explanation of the First Test Case:\n\nInput: `\"11000010001\"`\n\nLet's compute the running sum:\n\n| Index | Char | Value | Running Sum | Min Sum | Diff (Current - Min) |\n|-------|------|-------|-------------|---------|----------------------|\n| 0     | '1'  | -1    | -1          | -1      | 0                    |\n| 1     | '1'  | -1    | -2          | -2      | 0                    |\n| 2     | '0'  | +1    | -1          | -2      | 1                    |\n| 3     | '0'  | +1    | 0           | -2      | 2                    |\n| 4     | '0'  | +1    | 1           | -2      | 3                    |\n| 5     | '0'  | +1    | 2           | -2      | 4                    |\n| 6     | '1'  | -1    | 1           | -2      | 3                    |\n| 7     | '0'  | +1    | 2           | -2      | 4                    |\n| 8     | '0'  | +1    | 3           | -2      | 5                    |\n| 9     | '0'  | +1    | 4           | -2      | 6                    |\n| 10    | '1'  | -1    | 3           | -2      | 5                    |\n\nSo the maximum difference is **6**, which matches the expected result.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n```python\ndef find_length(s):\n    max_diff = 0\n    current_sum = 0\n    min_sum = 0\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            current_sum += 1\n        else:\n            current_sum -= 1\n\n        if current_sum - min_sum > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_sum - min_sum\n\n        if current_sum < min_sum:\n            min_sum = current_sum\n\n    return max_diff\n```", "decode_seconds": 4.100939109921455, "draft_calls": 110, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 134, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "48bff1be49b3fee1150a187a28c08be5dab65567aee1734d6b84d4edd12e1ee7", "method": "relay_activation1536", "output_hash"